#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1460
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Poll>poll</Poll> names the <GroupRole>roles</GroupRole> that vote, that see the results and that see the details, and the organizer and those who manage polls always see them. Once a <PollBallot>ballot</PollBallot> is in, what voters saw no longer changes, except the deadline. One account gives one vote, whichever of its profiles it uses, and a profile several accounts share votes on its own. A secret poll keeps no answers on its ballots, only the count of each <PollOption>answer</PollOption> grows, so neither the group's admins nor an app can see who voted for what. No counts show before its end, and a finished one is not opened again. A public poll also takes the votes of signed-in non-members of a public group. Deleting the <Value>value</Value> that carries a poll deletes the poll."
msgstr "<Poll>Glasanje</Poll> navodi <GroupRole>uloge</GroupRole> koje glasaju, koje vide rezultate i koje vide detalje, a organizator i oni koji upravljaju glasanjima ih vide uvek. Kad stigne prvi <PollBallot>listić</PollBallot>, ono što su glasači videli više se ne menja, osim roka. Jedan nalog daje jedan glas, kojim god svojim profilom, a profil koji deli više naloga glasa posebno. Tajno glasanje ne čuva odgovore na listićima, raste samo broj glasova svakog <PollOption>odgovora</PollOption>, pa ni admini grupe ni aplikacija ne vide ko je za šta glasao. Brojevi se ne vide pre kraja, a završeno se ne otvara ponovo. Javno glasanje prima i glasove prijavljenih nečlanova javne grupe. Brisanje <Value>vrednosti</Value> koja nosi glasanje briše i glasanje."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1524
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A new <Group>group</Group> can start from a preset: chat, folder, feed, polls, form, map or page. A preset sets what any group can have, so all of it can be changed later. The group keeps only the preset's name: its avatar shows that kind while the group still fits it, and the list of sub-groups can be narrowed to one kind. A feed is two groups, one with the Feed app and one below it with FeedCreator, and each keeps its own copy of its app, so a new version reaches only the feeds made after it. A group for polls, a form and a map keep a copy of their app the same way, and a form gets its two groups for files only once it needs them. The root offers no map, as it has one of its own."
msgstr "Nova <Group>grupa</Group> može da krene od preseta: chat, folder, feed, glasanja, forma, mapa ili stranica. Preset podešava ono što svaka grupa može da ima, pa se sve može kasnije promeniti. Grupa pamti samo ime preseta: njen avatar pokazuje tu vrstu dok joj grupa još odgovara, a lista podgrupa može da se suzi na jednu vrstu. Feed su dve grupe, jedna sa aplikacijom Feed i jedna ispod nje sa FeedCreator-om, i svaka čuva svoju kopiju aplikacije, pa nova verzija stiže samo u feed-ove napravljene posle nje. Grupa za glasanja, forma i mapa na isti način čuvaju kopiju svoje aplikacije, a forma svoje dve grupe za fajlove dobija tek kad joj zatrebaju. Koren ne nudi mapu, jer ima svoju."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1250
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A new value reaches right away, with no refresh, everyone who has the app open and may see it."
msgstr "Nova vrednost odmah stiže, bez osvežavanja, svakome ko ima otvorenu aplikaciju i sme da je vidi."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1268
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An app can keep its <Value>values</Value> under rules its editors set: which <GroupRole>roles</GroupRole> write and which read everything, one answer per person, changing one's own answer, a deadline, anonymous answers and, in a public group, answers from signed-in non-members. Potok also scores a quiz by a key only the editors see, counts the answers for a summary, keeps the files sent with them in two sub-groups of the app's group, and sends a push about each new answer to whoever asks for it. That is how a group becomes a form."
msgstr "Aplikacija može da čuva svoje <Value>vrednosti</Value> po pravilima koja postave njeni urednici: koje <GroupRole>uloge</GroupRole> upisuju, a koje čitaju sve, jedan odgovor po osobi, izmena svog odgovora, rok, anonimni odgovori i, u javnoj grupi, odgovori prijavljenih nečlanova. Potok uz to boduje kviz po ključu koji vide samo urednici, broji odgovore za rezime, fajlove poslate uz odgovore čuva u dve podgrupe grupe aplikacije i javlja svaki nov odgovor onome ko to zatraži. Tako grupa postaje forma."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1570
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An app's data carry their own rules"
msgstr "Podaci aplikacije nose svoja pravila"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1572
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An app's settings are one <Value>value</Value> of its own: the app's data, a secret part only its editors read, and the rules of its other collections, which Potok holds to on every call. A rule names the <GroupRole>roles</GroupRole> that write and those that read everything; everyone else reads only what they wrote, and those who may edit the group always read all. A collection without a rule is closed the same way. One answer per person counts one account once, as a poll does. An answer written while its collection was anonymous never shows its author to anyone but the author, though its time shows, and whoever rewrites the app's code could still get around it. Files sent with answers are values with a <ValueAttachment>file</ValueAttachment> in two sub-groups of the app's group: a closed one, whose members alone open them, and one that inherits the members. Whoever sent a file can always open it."
msgstr "Podešavanja aplikacije su jedna njena <Value>vrednost</Value>: podaci aplikacije, tajni deo koji čitaju samo njeni urednici i pravila ostalih njenih kolekcija, kojih se Potok drži pri svakom pozivu. Pravilo imenuje <GroupRole>uloge</GroupRole> koje upisuju i one koje čitaju sve. Svi ostali čitaju samo ono što su sami upisali, a oni koji smeju da uređuju grupu uvek čitaju sve. Kolekcija bez pravila je zatvorena na isti način. Jedan odgovor po osobi broji jedan nalog jednom, kao kod glasanja. Odgovor upisan dok je kolekcija bila anonimna nikome osim autoru ne pokazuje ko ga je napisao, mada se vidi kada je poslat, a ko prepiše kod aplikacije mogao bi to da zaobiđe. Fajlovi poslati uz odgovore su vrednosti sa <ValueAttachment>fajlom</ValueAttachment> u dve podgrupe grupe aplikacije: zatvorenoj, čiji ih članovi jedini otvaraju, i onoj koja nasleđuje članove. Onaj ko je fajl poslao uvek može da ga otvori."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1266
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Collects answers by its own rules"
msgstr "Skuplja odgovore po svojim pravilima"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1241
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Each app has its own <Value>values</Value>, apart from the other apps of the group. It can search them, sort them, count them, add them up and read them page by page, the newest first if it likes."
msgstr "Svaka aplikacija ima svoje <Value>vrednosti</Value>, odvojene od ostalih aplikacija u grupi. Može da ih pretražuje, sortira, broji, sabira i čita po stranicama, ako hoće i od najnovijih."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1259
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "It can also read the values of the group's other apps, except those kept under rules, and it writes only to its own."
msgstr "Može da čita i vrednosti ostalih aplikacija u grupi, osim onih koje se čuvaju po pravilima, a upisuje samo u svoje."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1389
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Members read and save values, and so do signed-in non-members where an app's rules open that to them in a public group. Rules can narrow it further, and the number of saves is limited."
msgstr "Vrednosti čitaju i upisuju članovi, a u javnoj grupi i prijavljeni nečlanovi, kad im to pravila aplikacije otvore. Pravila to mogu i dalje da suze, a broj upisa je ograničen."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1053
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only app data has a collection, named with small letters, digits, - and _."
msgstr "Kolekciju ima samo podatak aplikacije, a ime joj je od malih slova, cifara, - i _."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1397
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Potok checks who answers, when, how many times and how much, not what an answer says."
msgstr "Potok proverava ko odgovara, kada, koliko puta i koliko, a ne šta odgovor kaže."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1564
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The default description and every <GroupAltDescription>alternative description</GroupAltDescription> can be an app. Its data are <Value>values</Value> marked as data, and each of them knows which app it belongs to and which of the app's collections holds it. A composite key holds them in the same group, and deleting an alternative description deletes its data too."
msgstr "Podrazumevani opis i svaki <GroupAltDescription>alternativni opis</GroupAltDescription> mogu da budu aplikacija. Njeni podaci su <Value>vrednosti</Value> označene kao podaci, a svaka zna kojoj aplikaciji pripada i koja je kolekcija aplikacije drži. Složeni ključ ih drži u istoj grupi, a brisanje alternativnog opisa briše i njegove podatke."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:291
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "anonymous when written"
msgstr "anonimno pri upisu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:290
#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:307
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "collection of app data"
msgstr "kolekcija podataka aplikacije"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:292
#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:313
#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:357
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "revision"
msgstr "revizija"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:293
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "score and grades"
msgstr "bodovi i ocene"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:201
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "ready setup"
msgstr "gotova postavka"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1532
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Group>group</Group> can have a place: both coordinates or neither, set by whoever may edit it, with a pin picked from a list or the one of its kind, and a picked pin keeps the kind's mark in its corner, as the group's picture does. A map app shows the places of the groups right under its own, each to whoever sees that group. A group added from the map is an ordinary sub-group, made by whoever may make one there. The map's pictures come through Potok, so the map service does not see who is looking. The root has no map app but a map of its own: the places of every group the viewer sees, at any depth, which the server gathers into numbered circles where they stand close, narrowed by the filters of the sub-groups, by the pins the groups show and by when a group appeared or was last written in, at any time until the viewer picks a time frame. A search by a group's name, there and among the sub-groups, takes no notice of diacritics or of a name written in Latin or Cyrillic."
msgstr "<Group>Grupa</Group> može da ima mesto: obe koordinate ili nijednu, koje postavlja onaj ko sme da je uređuje, sa pinom izabranim sa liste ili onim njene vrste, a izabrani pin u uglu zadržava znak vrste, kao i slika grupe. Aplikacija mape prikazuje mesta grupa neposredno ispod svoje, svako onome ko tu grupu vidi. Grupa dodata sa mape je obična podgrupa, koju pravi onaj ko tu sme da napravi podgrupu. Slike mape dolaze preko Potoka, pa servis mapa ne vidi ko gleda. Koren nema aplikaciju mape nego svoju mapu: mesta svih grupa koje gledalac vidi, na bilo kojoj dubini, koja server skuplja u krugove sa brojem gde stoje blizu, sužena filterima podgrupa, pinovima koje grupe pokazuju i vremenom kad je grupa nastala ili kad je u njoj poslednji put pisano, u bilo koje vreme dok gledalac ne izabere period. Pretraga po imenu grupe, tu i među podgrupama, ne mari za kvačice ni za to da li je ime napisano latinicom ili ćirilicom."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1530
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group can stand on a map"
msgstr "Grupa može da stoji na mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:927
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A place on a map has both coordinates, each within its range, or neither."
msgstr "Mesto na mapi ima obe koordinate, svaku u njenom opsegu, ili nijednu."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1302
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Shows its groups on a map"
msgstr "Prikazuje svoje grupe na mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:202
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "latitude on a map"
msgstr "geografska širina na mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:203
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "longitude on a map"
msgstr "geografska dužina na mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:204
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "pin on a map"
msgstr "pin na mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1548
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Group>group</Group>'s place can be an area instead of a point, as a local community covers its streets: a border drawn on the map or brought from a GeoJSON file, set by whoever may edit the group. The area keeps a pin, which the server puts inside it by itself. An area holds a group when it holds that group's pin, so every place shows the areas around it, smallest first, and an area inside a bigger one lies in it too. Each viewer sees only the areas of the groups they see. On the root's map an area is only the shape of its group: the filters keep it or leave it out like any group, and once it is wide enough it also shows its border, under the pins. An area that holds others whose borders show inside it gets a wide soft band under every border, so its own border shows where theirs lie on it. A tap on the map lists the areas there, and a filter keeps only the groups inside chosen areas, which stay outlined."
msgstr "Mesto <Group>grupe</Group> može biti područje umesto tačke, kao što mesna zajednica pokriva svoje ulice: granica nacrtana na mapi ili uvezena iz GeoJSON fajla, a zadaje je ko sme da uređuje grupu. Područje zadržava pin, koji server sam stavlja unutar njega. Područje obuhvata grupu kad obuhvata njen pin, pa svako mesto pokazuje područja oko sebe, od najmanjeg, a područje unutar većeg i samo leži u njemu. Svako vidi samo područja grupa koje vidi. Na mapi korena područje je samo oblik svoje grupe: filteri ga zadrže ili izostave kao svaku grupu, a kad je dovoljno široko, pokazuje i svoju granicu, ispod pinova. Područje koje drži druga područja čije se granice vide u njemu dobija ispod svih granica širok providan pojas, pa mu se granica vidi i tamo gde se poklapa sa njihovim. Dodir na mapu nabraja područja na tom mestu, a filter ostavlja samo grupe unutar izabranih područja, koja ostaju uokvirena."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1546
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A place can be an area"
msgstr "Mesto može biti područje"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:938
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An area on a map always has its pin as well."
msgstr "Područje na mapi uvek ima i svoj pin."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:206
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "area on a map, as its border"
msgstr "područje na mapi, kao njegova granica"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:215
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "eastern edge of the area"
msgstr "istočna ivica područja"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:210
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "name as a search reads it, in Latin and without diacritics"
msgstr "ime kako ga pretraga čita, latinicom i bez kvačica"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:216
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "northern edge of the area"
msgstr "severna ivica područja"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:212
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "size of the area"
msgstr "veličina područja"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:214
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "southern edge of the area"
msgstr "južna ivica područja"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:213
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "western edge of the area"
msgstr "zapadna ivica područja"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:217
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "width of the area on a map"
msgstr "širina područja na mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1556
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Group>group</Group>'s place can also be a route, as a walk, a race, a march or a bike path runs: a line drawn on the map or brought from a GPX, KML or GeoJSON file, set by whoever may edit the group. A place is a point, an area or a route, never an area and a route at once. The route keeps its pin at its start, where people meet, which the server puts there by itself, and the map marks its end with a ring. A route lies in every area it passes through, not only in the one it starts in, so its page lists those areas and the filter by area keeps it. On the root's map a route is only the shape of its group, as an area is: the filters keep it or leave it out, and once it is wide enough its line is drawn over the areas, under the pins, in a layer of its own; a tap on the line opens the group, and a link to the map can show one route, whatever the filters."
msgstr "Mesto <Group>grupe</Group> može biti i ruta, onako kako idu šetnja, trka, protestni marš ili biciklistička staza: linija nacrtana na mapi ili uvezena iz GPX, KML ili GeoJSON fajla, a zadaje je ko sme da uređuje grupu. Mesto je tačka, područje ili ruta, nikad i područje i ruta u isto vreme. Ruta drži svoj pin na početku, gde se ljudi okupljaju, i server ga sam tamo stavlja, a mapa njen kraj obeležava kružićem. Ruta leži u svakom području kroz koje prolazi, ne samo u onom u kom počinje, pa njena stranica nabraja ta područja, a filter po području je zadržava. Na mapi korena ruta je samo oblik svoje grupe, kao i područje: filteri je zadrže ili izostave, a kad je dovoljno široka, njena linija se crta preko područja, ispod pinova, u posebnom sloju; dodir na liniju otvara grupu, a link ka mapi može da pokaže jednu rutu, kakvi god da su filteri."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1554
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A place can be a route"
msgstr "Mesto može biti ruta"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:942
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A route on a map always has its pin as well, and a place is never an area and a route at once."
msgstr "Ruta na mapi uvek ima i svoj pin, a mesto nikad nije i područje i ruta u isto vreme."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:224
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "eastern edge of the route"
msgstr "istočna ivica rute"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:220
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "length of the route, in metres"
msgstr "dužina rute, u metrima"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:225
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "northern edge of the route"
msgstr "severna ivica rute"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:207
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "route on a map, as its line"
msgstr "ruta na mapi, kao njena linija"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:223
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "southern edge of the route"
msgstr "južna ivica rute"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:222
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "western edge of the route"
msgstr "zapadna ivica rute"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:226
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "width of the route on a map"
msgstr "širina rute na mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1680
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An <Event>event</Event>'s place is words, and it can also stand on the map: at the place of a <Group>group</Group> or at a place of its own, never both. A place of its own is a point, an area or a route, as a group's is, drawn the same way, and an area or a route keeps its pin. Only a group with a place that the author sees can be picked, and the event then stands where the group stands, even after the group moves. Whoever does not see that group sees only the words, and deleting the group leaves the words as well. A link from a group or from an event opens the root's map on its place, which stands out whatever the filters, and an event shows a card of its own there."
msgstr "Mesto <Event>događaja</Event> su reči, a može da stoji i na mapi: na mestu neke <Group>grupe</Group> ili na svom mestu, nikad oboje. Svoje mesto je tačka, područje ili ruta, kao kod grupe, i crta se na isti način, a područje ili ruta zadržava svoj pin. Može da se izabere samo grupa sa mestom koju autor vidi, i događaj onda stoji gde i grupa, i kad se ona pomeri. Ko tu grupu ne vidi, vidi samo reči, a i brisanje grupe ostavlja reči. Link sa grupe ili sa događaja otvara mapu korena na tom mestu, koje se ističe kakvi god da su filteri, a događaj tamo pokazuje i svoju karticu."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1678
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An event can take place at a group"
msgstr "Događaj može da se održava u grupi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:967
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An event's point has both coordinates, each within its range, or neither, and an event at a group's place has no point of its own."
msgstr "Tačka događaja ima obe koordinate, svaku u njenom opsegu, ili nijednu, a događaj na mestu grupe nema svoju tačku."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:384
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "group it takes place at"
msgstr "grupa u kojoj se održava"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:385
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "latitude of its point"
msgstr "geografska širina tačke"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:386
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "longitude of its point"
msgstr "geografska dužina tačke"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:974
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An event's area or route always has its pin as well, and an event never has an area and a route at once."
msgstr "Područje ili ruta događaja uvek ima i svoj pin, a događaj nikad nema i područje i rutu u isto vreme."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:387
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "its area on a map, as its border"
msgstr "njegovo područje na mapi, kao granica"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:388
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "its route on a map, as its line"
msgstr "njegova ruta na mapi, kao linija"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:236
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "newest value, for a member"
msgstr "poslednja vrednost, za člana"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:274
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "text as a search reads it, in Latin and without diacritics"
msgstr "tekst kako ga pretraga čita, latinicom i bez kvačica"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1492
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <GroupValueRead>read marker</GroupValueRead> holds, for one profile in one group, the last <Value>value</Value> it has read, and everything newer is unread. Only members have one, and a chat opened while still empty gets one too. Opening the chat moves the marker to the newest value, and the line that shows where the unread values begin stands where the marker was before. A group's newest value shows in the lists only to its members, as only their pages hear of new values. A search of the chat finds what the chat shows: a member's also takes the threads it is in, and someone reading an open chat from outside does not find announcements of events that are not public."
msgstr "<GroupValueRead>Marker čitanja</GroupValueRead> čuva, za jedan profil u jednoj grupi, poslednju <Value>vrednost</Value> koju je pročitao, a sve novije je nepročitano. Imaju ga samo članovi, a dobija ga i razgovor otvoren dok je još prazan. Otvaranje razgovora pomera marker na najnoviju vrednost, a linija koja pokazuje gde počinju nepročitane vrednosti stoji tamo gde je marker bio pre toga. Najnovija vrednost grupe vidi se u listama samo njenim članovima, jer samo njihove stranice čuju za nove vrednosti. Pretraga razgovora nalazi ono što razgovor pokazuje: pretraga člana uzima i niti u kojima je, a ko čita otvoren razgovor spolja ne nalazi najave događaja koji nisu javni."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1490
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Unread is measured from one marker"
msgstr "Nepročitano se meri od jednog markera"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1466
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group sends notices to those who follow it"
msgstr "Grupa šalje obaveštenja onima koji je prate"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:815
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A notice a group sent to those who follow it: one text, never edited. It remembers who sent it, how many followers it reached and the preview of its first link. Deleting it deletes it for everyone who received it."
msgstr "Obaveštenje koje je grupa poslala onima koji je prate: jedan tekst, koji se nikad ne menja. Pamti ko ga je poslao, do koliko pratilaca je stiglo i pregled njegovog prvog linka. Brisanje ga briše svima koji su ga primili."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:822
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A notice that reached one profile, and whether it was read. It is written when the notice is sent, for every follower who sees the group then, so it stays after unfollowing. Unread ones make the counter of notices."
msgstr "Obaveštenje koje je stiglo do jednog profila, i da li je pročitano. Upisuje se kad se obaveštenje pošalje, za svakog pratioca koji tada vidi grupu, pa ostaje i kad pratilac prestane da prati grupu. Nepročitana čine brojač obaveštenja."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1468
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A profile can follow a <Group>group</Group> it sees, a public one without being a member: that is a <GroupFollow>following</GroupFollow>. The root, direct conversations and threads are not followed. Whoever holds the permission to send notices sends a <GroupNotice>notice</GroupNotice>, and `admin` holds it as it holds every permission. The notice is written as a <GroupNoticeReceipt>received notice</GroupNoticeReceipt> for every follower who sees the group at that moment, never for its author, so it stays after unfollowing, and a later follower finds the older ones on the group's page. Unread received notices make their own counter, apart from unread messages, and opening the list of notices or the group's notices reads them. A push goes out while both the following and the profile allow it. Deleting a notice takes it from everyone who received it. The preview of a notice's first link comes a moment after it is sent, and whoever may delete the notice may remove the preview, for everyone. At the root, the groups a profile follows stay on its lists and on the map of groups while the other public groups are hidden, and its sub-groups can be narrowed to them."
msgstr "Profil može da prati <Group>grupu</Group> koju vidi, javnu i kad nije njen član: to je <GroupFollow>praćenje</GroupFollow>. Koren, direktni razgovori i niti se ne prate. <GroupNotice>Obaveštenje</GroupNotice> šalje onaj ko ima dozvolu za slanje obaveštenja, a `admin` je ima kao i svaku dozvolu. Obaveštenje se upisuje kao <GroupNoticeReceipt>primljeno obaveštenje</GroupNoticeReceipt> za svakog pratioca koji u tom trenutku vidi grupu, nikad za njegovog autora, pa ostaje i kad pratilac prestane da prati grupu, a kasniji pratilac starija obaveštenja nalazi na stranici grupe. Nepročitana primljena obaveštenja imaju svoj brojač, odvojen od nepročitanih poruka, a otvaranje spiska obaveštenja ili obaveštenja grupe ih čita. Push notifikacija ide dok je dozvoljavaju i praćenje i profil. Brisanje obaveštenja ga uklanja svima koji su ga primili. Pregled prvog linka u obaveštenju stiže trenutak posle slanja, a ko sme da obriše obaveštenje, može da ukloni pregled, svima. U korenu grupe koje profil prati ostaju na spiskovima i na mapi grupa i kad su ostale javne grupe sakrivene, a podgrupe mogu da se suze na njih."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:808
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A profile follows a group, to receive its notices. Anyone who sees the group may follow it, a public one without being a member. It says whether the group's notices push to the follower's devices."
msgstr "Profil prati grupu da bi primao njena obaveštenja. Grupu može da prati svako ko je vidi, javnu i kad nije njen član. Pamti da li obaveštenja grupe idu kao push notifikacije na uređaje pratioca."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:593
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Following"
msgstr "Praćenje"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:559
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Following and notices"
msgstr "Praćenje i obaveštenja"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:594
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Notice"
msgstr "Obaveštenje"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:595
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Received notice"
msgstr "Primljeno obaveštenje"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1002
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The text has 1 to 2,000 characters, and not only spaces."
msgstr "Tekst ima od 1 do 2.000 znakova, i nisu svi razmaci."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:468
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "follower"
msgstr "pratilac"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:473
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "how many got it"
msgstr "koliko ih je primilo"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:477
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "notice"
msgstr "obaveštenje"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:180
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "push of notices"
msgstr "push za obaveštenja"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:469
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "push to devices"
msgstr "push na uređaje"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:478
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "read at"
msgstr "vreme čitanja"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:476
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "recipient"
msgstr "primalac"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:471
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "who sent it"
msgstr "ko ga je poslao"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1540
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Group>group</Group> an app made with a key of its own is a record, such as one row of an open dataset brought in with thousands of others. The key is set once and is unique under its parent, so bringing the same list in again makes no duplicates. A record is an ordinary group, seen by whoever may see it, but it stands only on its own map: the root's map and the place picker of events leave records out, and the unread counts of the profile that brought them in do not follow them. Pages hear of a hundred records made at once as of one change."
msgstr "<Group>Grupa</Group> koju je aplikacija napravila sa sopstvenim ključem je zapis, kao jedan red otvorenih podataka unet sa hiljadama drugih. Ključ se upisuje jednom i jedinstven je ispod roditelja, pa ponovni unos istog spiska ne pravi duplikate. Zapis je obična grupa, vidi je ko sme da je vidi, ali stoji samo na svojoj mapi: mapa korena i biranje mesta za događaje izostavljaju zapise, a nepročitano profila koji ih je uneo ne prati ih. Stranice za stotinu zapisa napravljenih odjednom saznaju kao za jednu promenu."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:934
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An app's key for a group has from 1 to 64 characters."
msgstr "Ključ aplikacije za grupu ima od 1 do 64 znaka."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1313
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "For a viewer who may edit its group, an app can make <Group>groups</Group> right under it, change them and take them back, and put them on a map with a pin. A new one opens its chat if the app's group has. It can also make up to a hundred at once, all or none, each with a key of its own, so that the same list brought in again makes no duplicates: that is how the rows of an open dataset become groups on a map. That is how one app writes what another shows, and a feed gets its editors' desk."
msgstr "Za gledaoca koji sme da menja njenu grupu, aplikacija pravi <Group>grupe</Group> odmah ispod sebe, menja ih, povlači i stavlja na mapu sa pinom. Nova otvara razgovor ako ga je otvorila grupa aplikacije. Može da napravi i do stotinu odjednom, sve ili nijednu, svaku sa sopstvenim ključem, pa ponovni unos istog spiska ne pravi duplikate: tako redovi otvorenih podataka postaju grupe na mapi. Tako jedna aplikacija piše ono što druga prikazuje, a feed dobija uredništvo."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1304
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "It gets the <Group>groups</Group> right under it that have a place on a map, with the pin each one shows, and whoever may make a sub-group there can add one where they tap. A tap on a pin opens that group's description over the app, where its own app, a form or a poll, works with that group's rights. Among them, groups that cover an area come with their borders, groups that run along a route with their lines and lengths, and each place with the areas it lies in or passes through, so the app draws the areas and routes and shows only the groups inside one area. A map of more than 2000 places gets only what its view shows, which the server gathers into numbered circles as on the root's map, filtered by name and by the pins the groups show. That is how a group becomes a map. The root needs no such app: it has a map of its own."
msgstr "Dobija <Group>grupe</Group> neposredno ispod sebe koje imaju mesto na mapi, sa pinom koji svaka pokazuje, a ko tu sme da pravi podgrupe može da doda novu tamo gde dodirne. Dodir na pin otvara opis te grupe preko aplikacije, gde njena aplikacija, forma ili glasanje, radi sa pravima te grupe. Među njima grupe koje pokrivaju područje stižu sa svojim granicama, grupe koje idu rutom sa njenom linijom i dužinom, a svako mesto sa područjima u kojima je ili kroz koja prolazi, pa aplikacija crta područja i rute i pokazuje samo grupe unutar jednog područja. Mapa sa više od 2000 mesta dobija samo ono što pokazuje njen pogled, a server to skuplja u numerisane krugove kao na mapi korena, uz filter po nazivu i po pinovima koje grupe pokazuju. Tako grupa postaje mapa. Korenu takva aplikacija ne treba: on ima svoju mapu."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1538
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Records stay on their own map"
msgstr "Zapisi ostaju na svojoj mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:205
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "an app's own key"
msgstr "ključ aplikacije"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:949
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A description only some roles see never goes to guests."
msgstr "Opis koji vide samo neke uloge nikad ne ide gostima."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1393
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A guest saves, reacts and votes in nothing. Of an app's values it gets only the settings and counts that public rules show everyone."
msgstr "Gost ništa ne čuva, ne reaguje i ne glasa. Od vrednosti aplikacije dobija samo podešavanja i rezime, kad ih javna pravila pokazuju svima."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1482
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A public group can open its description to guests"
msgstr "Javna grupa može da otvori opis i gostima"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1484
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Anyone with the link of a public <Group>group</Group> sees its name, its picture and a piece of its description, without an account. Whoever may edit the group can open the whole description to such guests, and then each <GroupAltDescription>alternative description</GroupAltDescription> marked for them goes along; one that only some <GroupRole>roles</GroupRole> see never does. A description that is an app runs for guests too, and only reads: the public groups below it, the descriptions of those open to guests, a map of them, public <Poll>polls</Poll> and what public rules show. The chat, the members and who reacted stay behind the login, and search engines do not list the page. A group that stops being public closes it, and keeps the choice for when it opens again."
msgstr "Svako ko ima link javne <Group>grupe</Group> vidi njen naziv, sliku i deo opisa, i bez naloga. Ko sme da uređuje grupu može takvim gostima da otvori ceo opis, i tada uz njega idu i <GroupAltDescription>alternativni opisi</GroupAltDescription> označeni za njih; onaj koji vide samo neke <GroupRole>uloge</GroupRole> nikad ne ide. Opis koji je aplikacija radi i za goste, i samo čita: javne grupe ispod sebe, opise onih otvorenih za goste, njihovu mapu, javna <Poll>glasanja</Poll> i ono što pokazuju javna pravila. Razgovor, članovi i ko je reagovao ostaju iza prijave, a pretraživači tu stranu ne prikazuju. Grupa koja prestane da bude javna zatvara je i pamti izbor za kad se ponovo otvori."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1374
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Opens to guests"
msgstr "Otvara se gostima"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1376
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Where a public <Group>group</Group> opens its description to guests, its app runs for people without an account too. It then lists the public groups below it and shows the descriptions of those open to guests, maps them and reads public <Poll>polls</Poll>, and a tap on a group opens its text over the app. That is how a feed or a map can be read by anyone with the link."
msgstr "Kad javna <Group>grupa</Group> otvori opis gostima, njena aplikacija radi i za ljude bez naloga. Tada nabraja javne grupe ispod sebe i pokazuje opise onih otvorenih za goste, stavlja ih na mapu i čita javna <Poll>glasanja</Poll>, a dodir na grupu otvara njen tekst preko aplikacije. Tako vesti ili mapu može da čita svako ko ima link."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:193
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "description open to guests"
msgstr "opis otvoren za goste"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:248
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "guests read it too"
msgstr "vide ga i gosti"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1064
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A month is written as its first day."
msgstr "Mesec se upisuje kao njegov prvi dan."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:885
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A technical table with no links to the rest of the domain: what one hour of one thing Potok runs on cost at `Fly.io`, a machine, the database, the stored files, the IP addresses or the data sent out, estimated by Potok itself from what `Fly.io` reports and its price list."
msgstr "Tehnička tabela bez veza sa ostatkom domena: koliko je na `Fly.io` koštao jedan sat jedne stvari na kojoj Potok radi, mašine, baze, sačuvanih fajlova, IP adresa ili poslatih podataka, kako ga Potok sam procenjuje iz onoga što `Fly.io` javlja i iz cenovnika."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:562
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Hosting costs"
msgstr "Troškovi hostinga"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:603
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Hour of costs"
msgstr "Sat troškova"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:604
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Invoice"
msgstr "Račun"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1060
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Neither the cost nor the amount is negative."
msgstr "Ni trošak ni količina nisu negativni."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1686
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Potok estimates what it costs"
msgstr "Potok procenjuje koliko košta"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1068
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The sum is not negative, and the note has up to 500 characters."
msgstr "Iznos nije negativan, a napomena ima najviše 500 znakova."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:892
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "What `Fly.io` actually billed for one month, copied from the invoice, so the estimate of that month stands next to the real sum."
msgstr "Koliko je `Fly.io` zaista naplatio za jedan mesec, prepisano sa računa, da procena tog meseca stoji pored pravog iznosa."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1688
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "`Fly.io` gives no way to read its bills, so Potok estimates them itself. Every quarter of an hour it reads which machines run and how big they are, how big the database and the stored files are and how much data went out, and writes what each <CostHour>hour</CostHour> cost by the price list. The hours it missed, back to the start of the month, are filled in from `Fly.io`'s own metrics of those hours, which go back about ten days, and the rest from what runs now. Once a month is billed, one of the people who run Potok copies the sum from the <Invoice>invoice</Invoice>, and only they may. Anyone sees both on the costs page, even without an account."
msgstr "`Fly.io` ne daje način da se pročitaju njegovi računi, pa ih Potok sam procenjuje. Na svakih petnaest minuta pročita koje mašine rade i koliko su velike, koliko su veliki baza i sačuvani fajlovi i koliko je podataka poslato, pa upiše koliko je svaki <CostHour>sat</CostHour> koštao po cenovniku. Sate koje je propustio, sve do početka meseca, popuni iz metrika samog `Fly.io` za te sate, koje sežu desetak dana unazad, a ostalo iz onoga što radi sada. Kad mesec bude naplaćen, neko od onih koji vode Potok prepiše iznos sa <Invoice>računa</Invoice>, i to smeju samo oni. Oboje svako vidi na strani sa troškovima, i bez naloga."

