#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1586
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A value sets an app's process going"
msgstr "Vrednost pokreće proces aplikacije"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1588
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "When a <Value>value</Value> comes to a collection whose process has a graph, a <ValueProcess>process instance</ValueProcess> starts in the same transaction, with a copy of the graph, so changing the rule later leaves it as it was. Each element runs in a transaction of its own together with the instance's move to the next, so what it writes happens once. The instance waits on a task until someone holding the task's role picks an outcome or the deadline passes, and on a timer until it is due; a scheduler on every server takes forward those whose time has come. An action that fails leaves the instance failed where it stopped, for an editor to take up again, and removing the rule cancels the instances that run or wait. Nobody learns from a process who wrote an anonymous value."
msgstr "Kad <Value>vrednost</Value> stigne u kolekciju čiji proces ima graf, u istoj transakciji nastaje <ValueProcess>instanca procesa</ValueProcess>, sa kopijom grafa, pa kasnija izmena pravila ne menja nju. Svaki element se izvršava u svojoj transakciji, zajedno sa pomeranjem instance na sledeći, pa ono što napiše nastaje jednom. Instanca čeka na zadatku dok neko sa ulogom zadatka ne izabere ishod ili ne istekne rok, a na tajmeru dok ne dođe vreme; Scheduler na svakom serveru pokreće one kojima je vreme došlo. Akcija koja ne uspe ostavlja instancu palu tamo gde je stala, da je urednik ponovo pokrene, a uklanjanje pravila otkazuje instance koje rade ili čekaju. Niko iz procesa ne saznaje ko je napisao anonimnu vrednost."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1275
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Runs a process"
msgstr "Vodi proces"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1277
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A collection's rule can carry the graph of a process, which Potok checks as the app saves it and runs for every new <Value>value</Value>: messages, sub-groups and pushes signed by the process's own <Profile>profile</Profile>, tasks for the people of a role, deadlines and timers. The app lists the <ValueProcess>instances</ValueProcess> of the values its viewer may read, lets whoever holds a task's role finish it, and lets its editors take a failed one up again or cancel one. Each move reaches the app live. Processes the group's editors draw in Potok on the same collection stay out of the app's sight: it neither lists nor finishes their instances."
msgstr "Pravilo kolekcije može da nosi graf procesa, koji Potok proverava kad ga aplikacija sačuva i izvršava za svaku novu <Value>vrednost</Value>: poruke, podgrupe i push koje potpisuje sopstveni <Profile>profil</Profile> procesa, zadatke za ljude jedne uloge, rokove i tajmere. Aplikacija prikazuje <ValueProcess>instance</ValueProcess> vrednosti koje gledalac sme da čita, pušta onoga ko ima ulogu zadatka da ga završi, a urednike da palu instancu ponovo pokrenu ili da otkažu neku. Svaki korak stiže u aplikaciju odmah. Procese koje urednici grupe nacrtaju u Potoku na istoj kolekciji aplikacija ne vidi: ne prikazuje njihove instance i ne završava njihove zadatke."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1594
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Editors can draw a process in Potok"
msgstr "Urednici mogu da nacrtaju proces u Potoku"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1014
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only a process drawn in Potok keeps a graph here."
msgstr "Graf ovde čuva samo proces nacrtan u Potoku."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:766
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The process of one collection of an app, with the profile that signs what it does and its owner, the editor who saved its rule. Removing the rule makes it inactive, and its profile stays as the author of what it wrote. A process an editor drew in Potok keeps its graph and the places of its steps here, where no save of the app reaches it; a collection has at most one process of the app's own, and may have drawn ones beside it."
msgstr "Proces jedne kolekcije aplikacije, sa profilom koji potpisuje ono što proces radi i vlasnikom, urednikom koji je sačuvao njegovo pravilo. Kad se pravilo ukloni, proces postaje neaktivan, a njegov profil ostaje autor onoga što je napisao. Proces koji je urednik nacrtao u Potoku ovde čuva svoj graf i mesta svojih koraka, gde ga čuvanje aplikacije ne dotiče. Kolekcija ima najviše jedan proces same aplikacije, a pored njega može da ima i nacrtane."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:310
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "drawn in Potok"
msgstr "nacrtan u Potoku"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:311
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "graph of a drawn process"
msgstr "graf nacrtanog procesa"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:312
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "places on the drawing"
msgstr "mesta na crtežu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:108
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "unless this holds: %{field}"
msgstr "osim kad važi: %{field}"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1018
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only a process that starts on a new value hangs on a collection."
msgstr "Samo proces koji počinje na novoj vrednosti vezan je za kolekciju."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:331
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "fields for its texts"
msgstr "polja za njegove tekstove"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:319
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "next scheduled start"
msgstr "sledeće pokretanje po rasporedu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:317
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "settings of what starts it"
msgstr "podešavanja okidača"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:329
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "sub-group that started it"
msgstr "podgrupa koja ga pokreće"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:314
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "what starts it"
msgstr "šta ga pokreće"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1026
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A process starts on a value, a message, a sub-group, a schedule, by hand, when another process calls it or on a signal."
msgstr "Proces počinje na vrednosti, poruci, podgrupi, po rasporedu, ručno, kad ga pozove drugi proces ili na signal."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1049
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A run is never less than zero processes deep."
msgstr "Pokretanje nikad nije manje od nula procesa duboko."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:745
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "One run of a process: the graph it started with, the element it stands on and when it wakes next. What set it going is a value of a collection or a chat message, a new sub-group, or nothing for a run started by hand or by a schedule, which keeps the fields its texts read. A run another process started, by a call or a signal, is one level deeper than that one, shares its subject and keeps the fields it was given; a caller that waits for it points at it, and what each wait brought back stays with the run that waited. A value or a sub-group has at most one instance of each process that its trigger started. Deleting it or the process takes the instance along, and what it wrote stays."
msgstr "Jedno pokretanje procesa: graf sa kojim je krenulo, element na kome stoji i kada se sledeći put budi. Pokrenula ga je vrednost iz kolekcije ili poruka u razgovoru, nova podgrupa, ili ništa, kad ga je neko pokrenuo ručno ili ga je pokrenuo raspored; tada čuva polja koja čitaju njegovi tekstovi. Pokretanje koje je pokrenuo drugi proces, pozivom ili signalom, jedan je nivo dublje od njega, ima isti predmet i čuva polja koja je dobilo; pozivalac koji ga čeka pokazuje na njega, a ono što je svako čekanje donelo ostaje uz pokretanje koje je čekalo. Vrednost ili podgrupa ima najviše jednu instancu svakog procesa koju je pokrenuo njegov okidač. Brisanje nje ili procesa briše i instancu, a ono što je napisala ostaje."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:360
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "how many processes deep"
msgstr "koliko procesa duboko"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:348
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "run it waits for"
msgstr "pokretanje koje čeka"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:363
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "what its waits brought back"
msgstr "šta su čekanja donela"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:111
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "where %{field} is %{value}"
msgstr "gde je %{field} %{value}"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1638
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Processes talk to each other only on purpose"
msgstr "Procesi razgovaraju samo namerno"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:752
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A field the processes drawn in a group keep for each other: a step sets it, or adds a number to it, and every drawn process of the group reads it. A group has at most 50, each name once. Deleting the group takes them along, and the process that wrote one last may go first."
msgstr "Polje koje procesi nacrtani u grupi čuvaju jedni za druge: korak ga postavlja ili mu dodaje broj, a čita ga svaki nacrtani proces grupe. Grupa ima najviše 50 polja, svako ime jednom. Brisanje grupe briše i njih, a proces koji je polje poslednji upisao može da nestane pre njega."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:585
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Group field"
msgstr "Polje grupe"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1033
#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1041
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The name has 1 to 40 characters."
msgstr "Ime ima od 1 do 40 znakova."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1037
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The text has at most 1,000 characters."
msgstr "Tekst ima najviše 1.000 znakova."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:352
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "process that wrote it last"
msgstr "ko ga je poslednji upisao"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:349
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "text it keeps"
msgstr "tekst koji čuva"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1516
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <GroupShortcut>shortcut</GroupShortcut> puts a <Group>group</Group> that stands deeper in the tree among the sub-groups of another group, the root as well, and a tap opens it where it stands. Whoever may make sub-groups there places one to a group they see, and it shows only to those who see that group, by the same rule as the other sub-groups. The row shows the group itself, with its newest value and what is unread in it, but the counts above it hold that unread once, where the group stands. It never leads to the root, a thread, a direct conversation or an app's record, nor to a group already standing there. Its author or an admin of the group it stands in removes it, which leaves the group as it is. Apps do not see shortcuts among the sub-groups."
msgstr "<GroupShortcut>Prečica</GroupShortcut> stavlja <Group>grupu</Group> koja stoji dublje u stablu među podgrupe druge grupe, pa i korena, a dodir je otvara tamo gde stoji. Postavlja je onaj ko tu sme da pravi podgrupe, do grupe koju vidi, a vide je samo oni koji vide tu grupu, po istom pravilu kao i ostale podgrupe. Red pokazuje samu grupu, sa njenom najnovijom vrednošću i onim što je u njoj nepročitano, ali brojači iznad njega to nepročitano broje jednom, tamo gde grupa stoji. Nikad ne vodi do korena, niti, direktnog razgovora ili zapisa aplikacije, ni do grupe koja već tu stoji. Uklanja je njen autor ili admin grupe u kojoj stoji, a grupa ostaje kakva je. Aplikacije ne vide prečice među podgrupama."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:731
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group shown among the sub-groups of another group too, as a shortcut on a computer: a tap opens it where it stands. It has no members, values or counts of its own. Deleting either group takes it along."
msgstr "Grupa prikazana i među podgrupama druge grupe, kao prečica na računaru: dodir je otvara tamo gde stoji. Nema svoje članove, vrednosti ni brojače. Brisanje bilo koje od te dve grupe briše i nju."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:923
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A shortcut never opens the group it stands in."
msgstr "Prečica nikad ne otvara grupu u kojoj stoji."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1514
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A shortcut shows a group in one more place"
msgstr "Prečica pokazuje grupu na još jednom mestu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:581
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Shortcut"
msgstr "Prečica"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:380
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "group it opens"
msgstr "grupa koju otvara"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:379
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "group it stands in"
msgstr "grupa u kojoj stoji"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:237
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "shortcut it is listed by"
msgstr "prečica u listi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:586
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Entity definition"
msgstr "Definicija entiteta"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1045
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The attributes are kept as a list."
msgstr "Atributi se čuvaju kao lista."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:355
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "attributes and their types"
msgstr "atributi i njihovi tipovi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:759
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "What the data of the processes drawn in a group looks like, as its editors define it: a name and up to 30 attributes, each with the type of what it holds. An attribute holds a text, a number, a yes or no, a date, a date and time, one of the choices it lists, or another entity of the group, and may be a list of them. Entities nest at most four deep and never in a circle. A group has at most 50, each name once in any letter case, and one that another holds, or that a process drawn in the group keeps a variable of, cannot be deleted. Deleting the group takes them along."
msgstr "Kako izgledaju podaci procesa nacrtanih u grupi, onako kako ih njeni urednici definišu: ime i najviše 30 atributa, svaki sa tipom onoga što sadrži. Atribut sadrži tekst, broj, da ili ne, datum, datum i vreme, jedan od izbora koje navodi ili drugi entitet grupe, a može da bude i lista. Entiteti se ugnežđuju najviše četiri nivoa duboko i nikad ukrug. Grupa ima najviše 50 entiteta, svako ime jednom, bez obzira na velika i mala slova, a entitet koji drugi sadrži, ili čiju varijablu čuva proces nacrtan u grupi, ne može da se obriše. Brisanje grupe briše i njih."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:365
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "what its variables hold"
msgstr "šta mu varijable drže"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1604
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <AppProcess>process</AppProcess> drawn in Potok that starts on a call, on a signal, by hand or on a value may take an <GroupEntity>entity</GroupEntity> of its group. A call then hands it that entity's attributes, each a value of its type and every required one a value, checked when the caller is saved and again when the call is made, against the entity as the called process was saved with it; a call that does not fit fails where it stands and starts nothing. A process started by hand asks for the attributes in a form, which is why it takes only an entity of plain attributes. A signal is waited for with an entity, and a process sends it only with the entity those who wait for it expect, where someone does: whoever waits says what it waits for. A drawing whose entity changed since it was saved, or whose calls and signals no longer fit those they talk to, runs on as it was saved, and its editors are told to look it over."
msgstr "Nacrtan <AppProcess>proces</AppProcess> koji počinje na poziv, na signal, ručno ili na vrednost može da prima <GroupEntity>entitet</GroupEntity> svoje grupe. Poziv mu tada predaje atribute tog entiteta, svakom vrednost njegovog tipa i svakom obaveznom neku vrednost, što se proverava kad se pozivalac čuva i ponovo kad se poziv desi, prema entitetu kakav je bio kad je pozvani proces sačuvan; poziv koji ne odgovara pada tu gde stoji i ne pokreće ništa. Proces koji se pokreće ručno atribute traži u formi, pa zato prima samo entitet sa običnim atributima. Signal se čeka sa entitetom, a proces ga šalje samo sa entitetom koji očekuju oni koji ga čekaju, ako takvih ima: ko čeka, kaže šta čeka. Crtež čiji se entitet promenio otkad je sačuvan, ili čiji pozivi i signali više ne odgovaraju onima sa kojima razgovara, radi kako je sačuvan, a njegovim urednicima se kaže da ga pregledaju."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1602
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "What a process takes is an entity"
msgstr "Ono što proces prima je entitet"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:320
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "entity it takes"
msgstr "entitet koji prima"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1596
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Besides the process an app writes into its rules, the editors of a group can draw processes of their own in Potok, as <AppProcess>app processes</AppProcess> that keep their graph outside any app's settings. One starts on a new value of a collection of an app, on a member's chat message holding one of its words or mentioning its role, on a sub-group made one at a time (not a record, a thread or what a process makes), on a schedule, when someone holding its role starts it by hand with a title and a text, when another process drawn in the group calls it, or on a signal one sends. An app replaces its settings whole when it saves them, so it could never keep a drawing safe; this way it neither sees nor overwrites them, and its own process runs beside them. A drawing is kept only when an instance could finish it, with roles the group has, and starts switched off. What its texts and conditions say are expressions over the names it has, such as what set it going and what a decision ended with, checked when it is kept, so a drawing that names what is not there is refused. One kept before expressions is turned into them when its editor opens it, and an instance reads the language of the graph it started with. A drawing may also declare variables, each with the type of what it holds, a plain one or an <GroupEntity>entity</GroupEntity> of the group: a step sets one to what an expression gives, every instance keeps its own, and the drawing is kept with the entities as they were then, so an instance under way reads them the same after one changes. A step may also go through a list an item at a time, with steps of its own for each: it reads the list once, on its way in, at most 200 items, and hands each to those steps by a name. So that a drawing that runs in a circle stops, an instance takes at most 25 steps in a row without waiting, counted anew for each item, and 5,000 in its life; after 100 it gives way to the others, and the steps that write outside it (a message, a sub-group, a push, a field of the group, a signal, a call) are 60 a minute for a process at most. Switched on, its profile joins the group and each of these starts a <ValueProcess>process instance</ValueProcess> of it; a change applies to the instances that start after it, and switching it off cancels those that run or wait. The app knows nothing of their tasks, so the people of a task's role finish them on the group's Processes tab, where they see a <Value>value</Value> only as far as they may read it. Deleting the app takes the processes drawn on its collections along."
msgstr "Pored procesa koji aplikacija upisuje u svoja pravila, urednici grupe mogu u Potoku da nacrtaju i svoje procese, kao <AppProcess>procese aplikacije</AppProcess> čiji graf stoji van podešavanja bilo koje aplikacije. Takav proces počinje na novoj vrednosti u kolekciji aplikacije, na poruci člana u razgovoru koja ima neku od njegovih reči ili pominje njegovu ulogu, na podgrupi napravljenoj jedna po jedna (ne na zapisu, niti ni onome što napravi proces), po rasporedu, kad ga neko sa njegovom ulogom pokrene ručno, uz naslov i tekst, kad ga pozove drugi proces nacrtan u grupi, ili na signal koji neki pošalje. Aplikacija pri čuvanju zameni cela podešavanja, pa crtež tamo ne bi bio bezbedan. Ovako ga aplikacija ne vidi i ne može da ga pregazi, a njen proces radi pored nacrtanih. Čuva se samo crtež koji instanca može da završi, sa ulogama koje grupa ima, i nastaje isključen. Ono što njegovi tekstovi i uslovi kažu su izrazi nad imenima koja proces ima, kao što su ono što ga je pokrenulo i ishod odluke, i proveravaju se pri čuvanju, pa se crtež koji imenuje nešto čega nema odbija. Crtež sačuvan pre izraza prevodi se u njih kad ga urednik otvori, a instanca čita zapis grafa sa kojim je krenula. Crtež može da ima i varijable, svaku sa tipom onoga što drži, običnim ili <GroupEntity>entitetom</GroupEntity> grupe: korak varijabli daje ono što izraz izračuna, svaka instanca ima svoje, a crtež se čuva sa entitetima kakvi su tada bili, pa ih instanca u toku čita isto i kad se neki promeni. Korak može i da prođe kroz listu, stavku po stavku, sa svojim koracima za svaku: listu čita jednom, kad u nju uđe, najviše 200 stavki, i svaku tim koracima daje pod imenom. Da bi crtež koji se vrti ukrug stao, instanca pravi najviše 25 koraka zaredom bez čekanja, što se za svaku stavku broji iznova, i 5.000 za svog veka; posle 100 ustupa mesto drugima, a koraka koji pišu van nje (poruka, podgrupa, push, polje grupe, signal, poziv) proces ima najviše 60 u minutu. Kad se uključi, njegov profil ulazi u grupu, a svaki od tih događaja pokreće njegovu <ValueProcess>instancu procesa</ValueProcess>. Izmena važi za instance koje krenu posle nje, a isključivanje otkazuje one koje rade ili čekaju. Aplikacija ne zna za njihove zadatke, pa ih ljudi sa ulogom zadatka završavaju na kartici Procesi u grupi, gde <Value>vrednost</Value> vide samo koliko smeju da je čitaju. Brisanje aplikacije briše i procese nacrtane na njenim kolekcijama."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1632
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A drawn <AppProcess>process</AppProcess> that others call is private until an editor makes it public. A private one is called by the processes of its own <Group>group</Group> alone. A public one is called from the groups above its group and from those below it too, never from a branch beside it, and the editors there see its name and what it takes. The <ValueProcess>run</ValueProcess> such a call starts in another group gets what the call hands over and nothing else: it has no subject and nobody set it off, as the caller's value and people are no part of that group, and the caller hears only which end it reached. Callers of other groups do not keep a public process from being deleted or made private again: their calls then fail where they stand, their editors are told to look the drawing over, and a caller left waiting for a run that went with its group fails as one whose run was cancelled."
msgstr "Nacrtan <AppProcess>proces</AppProcess> koji drugi pozivaju privatan je dok ga urednik ne učini javnim. Privatan pozivaju samo procesi njegove <Group>grupe</Group>. Javan pozivaju i procesi grupa iznad njegove grupe i onih ispod nje, nikad iz grane pored, a urednici tamo vide njegovo ime i šta prima. <ValueProcess>Pokretanje</ValueProcess> koje takav poziv napravi u drugoj grupi dobija ono što mu poziv preda i ništa više: nema predmet i niko ga nije pokrenuo, jer vrednost i ljudi pozivaoca nisu deo te grupe, a pozivalac saznaje samo do kog kraja je stiglo. Pozivaoci iz drugih grupa ne sprečavaju da se javan proces obriše ili ponovo postane privatan: njihovi pozivi tada padaju tu gde stoje, njihovim urednicima se kaže da pregledaju crtež, a pozivalac koji je ostao da čeka pokretanje nestalo sa svojom grupom pada kao onaj čije je pokretanje otkazano."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1627
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A process is private to its group, or public up and down the tree"
msgstr "Proces je privatan u svojoj grupi, ili javan uz i niz stablo"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1022
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only a process drawn in Potok that another calls can be public."
msgstr "Javan može da bude samo proces nacrtan u Potoku koji drugi poziva."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1640
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "What a process writes starts no other process: its messages and the sub-groups it makes set nothing going, so two processes never keep each other running by chance. A drawn process talks to another only by a step drawn for it. A call starts a drawn <AppProcess>process</AppProcess> that starts when another calls it, of the same group or a public one of a group above or below, and hands over what it takes; the <ValueProcess>run</ValueProcess> it starts is one level deeper, and in its own group it shares the caller's subject. A caller that waits goes on when that run ends, knowing which end it reached, or gives up at its deadline and cancels it. Cancelling a run cancels the run it waits for, and a run whose called run is cancelled stops, for an editor to take up again, which calls anew. A step can also keep a <GroupField>field of the group</GroupField>, which every drawn process of the group reads; adding to one takes its lock, so two runs never lose each other's count. A signal wakes the runs of the group's drawn processes that wait for it just then, at most 100, and starts the processes that start on it; nothing keeps it for a run that comes to wait later, and a wait may take only a signal sent on its own subject. Runs go at most three processes deep, and a process another one of its group calls cannot be deleted."
msgstr "Ono što proces napiše ne pokreće druge procese: njegove poruke i podgrupe koje napravi ne pokreću ništa, pa dva procesa nikad ne teraju jedan drugi slučajno. Nacrtan proces razgovara sa drugim samo korakom nacrtanim za to. Poziv pokreće nacrtan <AppProcess>proces</AppProcess> koji kreće kad ga drugi pozove, iz iste grupe ili javan iz grupe iznad ili ispod, i predaje mu ono što on prima; <ValueProcess>pokretanje</ValueProcess> koje tako krene jedan je nivo dublje, a u svojoj grupi ima isti predmet kao pozivalac. Pozivalac koji čeka ide dalje kad se to pokretanje završi, znajući do kog kraja je stiglo, ili na roku odustaje i otkazuje ga. Otkazivanje pokretanja otkazuje i ono koje ono čeka, a pokretanje čiji je pozvani proces otkazan staje, dok ga urednik ne pokrene ponovo, i tada poziva iznova. Korak može i da čuva <GroupField>polje grupe</GroupField>, koje čita svaki nacrtani proces grupe; dodavanje zaključava polje, pa dva pokretanja nikad ne izgube tuđe brojanje. Signal budi pokretanja nacrtanih procesa grupe koja ga baš tada čekaju, najviše 100, i pokreće procese koji kreću na njega; ništa ga ne čuva za pokretanje koje kasnije stigne do čekanja, a čekanje može da primi samo signal poslat o svom predmetu. Pokretanja idu najviše tri procesa duboko, a proces koji poziva drugi proces njegove grupe ne može da se obriše."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:371
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "person its wait asks"
msgstr "osoba koju čekanje pita"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:368
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "role its wait asks"
msgstr "uloga koju čekanje pita"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1618
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A process asks a person with a form"
msgstr "Proces pita čoveka formom"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1620
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A step of a drawing may be a form: it stops the <ValueProcess>process instance</ValueProcess> until a person fills in an <GroupEntity>entity</GroupEntity> of plain attributes, each as its type, as the drawing was saved with it. It may say something first, and start with something in some attributes, worked out from what the instance holds when the form is opened; the person may change it, and what they send counts. It asks whoever started the instance, or the people of a role, and only a member of the group answers, once. The form opens by itself only for the one who started the instance, and only when it was their own step that led to it: a message they wrote, a start by hand, a form before it. Reached after a wait or someone else's decision, and for a role, it waits on the group's Processes tab. What was filled in is read by the steps that follow, an attribute at a time, with who filled it in, and whoever filled it in sets off those steps. Nobody starts a process on a schedule, so its form asks a role, and an instance nobody started fails on a form that asks whoever did. While it waits for a person, on a form or a decision, an instance keeps whom it asks, so a group's page counts what waits for its viewer without reading every waiting instance, and counts again only on news that is theirs. The same count stands on the bar's hand beside the join requests the person may approve, the Requests page lists those tasks by group, and an amber mark stands on the rows of the groups they wait in and of those above them."
msgstr "Korak crteža može biti forma: zaustavlja <ValueProcess>instancu procesa</ValueProcess> dok čovek ne popuni <GroupEntity>entitet</GroupEntity> sa običnim atributima, svaki po svom tipu, onakav sa kakvim je crtež sačuvan. Može prvo nešto da kaže, a u nekim atributima već nešto može da bude upisano, izračunato iz onoga što instanca ima kad se forma otvori; čovek to može da promeni, a važi ono što pošalje. Pita onoga ko je instancu pokrenuo, ili ljude neke uloge, a odgovara samo član grupe, jednom. Forma se sama otvara samo onome ko je instancu pokrenuo, i samo kad je do nje doveo njegov korak: poruka koju je napisao, ručno pokretanje, forma pre nje. Kad do nje dođe posle čekanja ili tuđe odluke, i kad pita ulogu, čeka na kartici Procesi u grupi. Ono što je popunjeno čitaju koraci koji slede, atribut po atribut, uz to ko je popunio, a ko je popunio pokreće te korake. Proces po rasporedu ne pokreće niko, pa njegova forma pita ulogu, a instanca koju niko nije pokrenuo pada na formi koja pita pokretača. Dok čeka čoveka, na formi ili na odluci, instanca pamti koga pita, pa stranica grupe broji šta čeka onoga ko je gleda bez čitanja svake instance koja čeka, i broji ponovo samo na vest koja je njegova. Isti broj stoji na ruci u gornjoj traci, uz zahteve za pristup koje čovek može da odobri, stranica Zahtevi nabraja te zadatke po grupama, a ćilibarna oznaka stoji na redovima grupa u kojima čekaju i onih iznad njih."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1500
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <GroupMembership>membership</GroupMembership> remembers until when its member silenced the group: an hour, eight hours, a week or until they turn it on again. Until then nothing that goes to everyone reaches them as a push: new values, polls, events, an app's notices, a process's push to everyone. What is meant for them still does: a mention, an answer to their value, a reaction, a process asking them or their role. The group's unread values leave the home badge and the sums of the groups above it, while its own row still shows them, in grey. The threads of a silenced group are silent too."
msgstr "<GroupMembership>Članstvo</GroupMembership> pamti do kada je član utišao grupu: na sat vremena, osam sati, nedelju dana ili dok je ponovo ne uključi. Do tada mu nijedan push koji ide svima ne stiže: nove vrednosti, glasanja, događaji, obaveštenja aplikacije, push procesa svima. Ono što je namenjeno njemu i dalje stiže: pominjanje, odgovor na njegovu vrednost, reakcija, proces koji pita njega ili njegovu ulogu. Nepročitane vrednosti grupe izlaze iz broja na kućici i iz zbirova grupa iznad nje, a njen red ih i dalje pokazuje, sivo. Utišana grupa utišava i svoje niti."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1498
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A member can silence a group"
msgstr "Član može da utiša grupu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:374
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "until when the member silenced it"
msgstr "do kada je član utišao grupu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1612
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <AppProcess>process</AppProcess> that others call may name an <GroupEntity>entity</GroupEntity> of its group that it hands back. Each of its ends then fills it in, an attribute at a time, checked when the process is saved, and the caller reads it under the call's id, in its own group or in another: the process hands over exactly that and nothing else. One that names none hands back only the end it reached, and to a caller of its own group what it was given and what its waits brought back. An end whose values do not fit when the run gets there fails that run, and the caller waits for it as for any run it called."
msgstr "<AppProcess>Proces</AppProcess> koji drugi pozivaju može da navede <GroupEntity>entitet</GroupEntity> svoje grupe koji vraća. Tada ga svaki njegov kraj popunjava, atribut po atribut, što se proverava kad se proces sačuva, a pozivalac ga čita pod id-jem poziva, u svojoj grupi ili u drugoj: proces predaje tačno to i ništa više. Proces koji ne navede nijedan vraća samo kraj do kog je stigao, a pozivaocu iz svoje grupe i ono što je dobio i ono što su mu čekanja donela. Kraj čije vrednosti ne odgovaraju kad tok stigne do njega obara taj tok, a pozivalac ga čeka kao svaki tok koji je pozvao."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1610
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A called process can hand an entity back"
msgstr "Pozvani proces može da vrati entitet"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:323
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "entity it hands back"
msgstr "entitet koji vraća"
